  "341525": {
    "id": 341525,
    "literal_statement": "Let $u_\\mathbb{P}(q;n)$ be the counting quasipolynomial for nonattacking configurations of $q$ copies of a two-move rider $\\mathbb{P}$ on the dilated unit board, and let $D([0,1]^{2q},\\mathcal{A}_\\mathbb{P}^q)$ be the denominator of the associated inside-out polytope. The period of $u_\\mathbb{P}(q;n)$ is the shortest length of its cyclic sequence of constituent polynomials. **Period-denominator equality conjecture.** The period of the counting quasipolynomial $u_\\mathbb{P}(q;n)$ equals the denominator\n\n$$\nD([0,1]^{2q},\\mathcal{A}_\\mathbb{P}^q).\n$$\n\nThe period always divides the denominator by Ehrhart theory, but equality is generally surprising because periods can be smaller than denominators; this conjecture asserts equality for these chess-piece counting quasipolynomials.",
