    "literal_statement": "A regular CW sphere is a regular CW complex whose underlying space is a sphere, and its $cd$-index is the polynomial $\\Phi_P(c,d)$ encoding its flag $f$-vector, with $c$ of degree $1$ and $d$ of degree $2$. **Nonnegativity conjecture.** The coefficients in the $cd$-index of every regular CW sphere are nonnegative. This extends the nonnegativity known for convex polytopes to all regular CW spheres; the source gives no resolution of the conjecture.",
