    "literal_statement": "Let $\\mathcal{M}=\\{1^2,2^2,\\ldots,n^2\\}$, and let $\\overline{\\mathcal{Q}}_{\\mathcal{M}}$ denote the set of quasi-Stirling permutations of $\\mathcal{M}$. For a permutation $\\pi=\\pi_1\\pi_2\\ldots\\pi_{2n}$, define\n\n$$\ndes(\\pi)=|\\{i\\mid \\pi_i>\\pi_{i+1},\\ 1\\leq i\\leq 2n-1\\}|+1.\n$$\n\n**Archer et al.'s conjecture.** The number of $\\pi\\in\\overline{\\mathcal{Q}}_{\\mathcal{M}}$ with $des(\\pi)=n$ is equal to\n\n$$\n(n+1)^{n-1}.\n$$\n\nThis conjecture concerns the descent enumerator of quasi-Stirling permutations on the multiset in which every element occurs twice. It refines the known enumeration $|\\overline{\\mathcal{Q}}_{\\mathcal{M}}|=n!C_n$, where $C_n$ is the $n$th Catalan number; the supplied text gives no evidence that the descent-count assertion has been resolved.",
