  "363274": {
    "id": 363274,
    "literal_statement": "Let $P$ be a $(3+1)$-free poset, let $v\\in P$, and let $P_v$ be the poset obtained by adding an element $v'$ that is incomparable to $w$ if and only if either $w=v$ or $w$ is incomparable to $v$. Let $\\operatorname{Inc}(P)$ denote the incomparability graph of $P$.\n\n**Foley–Hoàng–Merkel's twinning conjecture.** If $P$ is $(3+1)$-free and $X_{\\operatorname{Inc}(P)}(\\mathbf{x})$ is $e$-positive, then $X_{\\operatorname{Inc}(P_v)}(\\mathbf{x})$ is $e$-positive for any $v\\in P$.\n\nThis is a weakened version of the Stanley–Stembridge conjecture, motivated by the fact that twinning preserves the property of being $(3+1)$-free. The source does not state that this conjecture has been resolved.",
